From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:18:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Yandex: per-account chunk size, gap-fill scans only
 unarchived UIDs, wait before reconnect

- Account field imap_fetch_chunk_kb (create/update/view): None = server
  default (BICHON_IMAP_FETCH_CHUNK_KB), 0 = off, N = KB per part;
  clear_imap_fetch_chunk_kb resets it. Additive serde field, no migration.
  Web UI: "Chunk size" in the account's download settings and details,
  en/ru strings, schema test; CI runs the account UI tests.
- Gap-fill: with an unchanged UIDVALIDITY only UIDs not archived in the
  folder go through the header comparison (unchanged::uids_to_scan); the
  local snapshot is taken before the scan. A changed UIDVALIDITY keeps the
  full comparison.
- Every reconnect after a dropped connection now waits before the new
  LOGIN (imap/reconnect.rs, BICHON_IMAP_RECONNECT_DELAYS, default
  30,60,120 s): Yandex drops a LOGIN right after a drop.
- Tests: account API roundtrip, uids_to_scan, reconnect delays; upstream
  download and gap-fill tests still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
